{
  "phase": "bounded-native-progressive-frame-cache-loading",
  "date": "2026-10-08",
  "source_commit": "b69eca232217360cf1502ef0223523d818606652",
  "scope": "Count-bearing native receipts, one-slot actual source Step loading, atomic replay state and explicit IO/host observations.",
  "behavior_contract": [
    "Original serialized slot count survives sparse and trailing noone holes. Cache completes at current project frame count; Cache Array at original inventory length.",
    "Native Begin initializes metadata only. Each actual Step decodes its selected slot; future pixels remain unallocated. Evaluation reads never advance progress.",
    "Paused loading and direct completion update follow source overrides. Cache Array paused completion retains its constructor output until playing update.",
    "Clear preserves loading cursor and pending inventory. Loading survives Serialize changes after constructor admission.",
    "Admission rejects malformed future publication, missing count, out-of-range source slots, malformed packets and aggregate byte overruns atomically.",
    "Prepared inventories and import layouts are explicit caller observations. Native v1 remains complete-playback compatible but cannot supply progressive count proof."
  ],
